Package: newmark
Type: Package
Title: Uncertainty Analysis in Dynamic Site and Slope Response
Version: 1.9.0
Authors@R: 
    person(given = "Alejandro",
           family = "Verri Kozlowski",
           email = "averri@fi.uba.ar",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Estimates the seismic response of sites and slopes from the
    results of a seismic hazard analysis. For a site, it computes the
    fundamental period of the soil profile and the amplification of
    spectral acceleration. For a slope, it computes the fundamental
    period, the earthquake-induced displacement, and the pseudostatic
    coefficient that keeps a selected quantile of the displacement
    within a given limit. Uncertainty in the soil profile and in the
    ground motion is represented by Monte Carlo samples. Every result is
    reported with its representative value, its applicable quantiles or
    dispersion, and the population or conditioning to which it refers.
